  "verified_at": null,
  "note": "Compiled for Remorsearch UX QA; not transcribed from any other project. Words match case-insensitively; ASCII markers match only at identifier boundaries (a letter or digit may not touch either end), a space inside a marker matches any run of whitespace (none for Korean). Word markers count only on pages with thin main content, and only as notices: outside navigation chrome and links, not quoted, asked about or written as a person's own report (verdict.py). Structural markers (widgets, inputs, script sources, password fields) are checked first. Promotion markers are disclosure forms, not bare words, so a complaint about sponsored posts is not itself flagged; the flags they raise are candidates that a verifier confirms before a grade is capped. Injection patterns are regular expressions; credential and command patterns need a request addressed to the reader.",
